    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "第三次估计将2024年第三季度美国实际GDP年化增长率从第二次估计的2.8%上调至3.1%。",
        "kind": "model_interpretation",
        "citations": [
          {
            "source_id": "source_20bd17ab9d75424aafe5b33229d32d43",
            "location": {
              "character_start": 371,
              "character_end": 476,
              "page": 1
            },
            "quotation_match": "whitespace_normalized",
            "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
            "quotation": "Real gross domestic product (GDP) increased at an annual rate of 2.8 percent in the third quarter of\n2024"
          },
          {
            "source_id": "source_308d821886f74e75a89a603716e5e21e",
            "location": {
              "character_start": 386,
              "character_end": 536,
              "page": 1
            },
            "quotation_match": "whitespace_normalized",
            "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
            "quotation": "Real gross domestic product (GDP) increased at an annual rate of 3.1 percent in the third quarter of\n2024 (table 1), according to the \"third\" estimate"
          }
        ],
        "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
        "role": "support"
      },
      {
        "text": "两份估计均采用经季节调整的年化增长率口径。",
        "kind": "model_interpretation",
        "citations": [
          {
            "source_id": "source_20bd17ab9d75424aafe5b33229d32d43",
            "location": {
              "character_start": 1417,
              "character_end": 1482,
              "page": 1
            },
            "quotation_match": "exact",
            "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
            "quotation": "U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis Seasonally adjusted annual rates"
          }
        ],
        "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
        "role": "support"
      },
      {
        "text": "上调的原因主要是出口和消费者支出的上调，但被私人存货投资的下调部分抵消。",
        "kind": "model_interpretation",
        "citations": [
          {
            "source_id": "source_308d821886f74e75a89a603716e5e21e",
            "location": {
              "character_start": 843,
              "character_end": 1003,
              "page": 1
            },
            "quotation_match": "whitespace_normalized",
            "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
            "quotation": "The update primarily reflected upward revisions to exports and consumer spending that were partly\noffset by a downward revision to private inventory investment."
          }
        ],
        "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
        "role": "support"
      },
      {
        "text": "第二次估计本身较先行估计持平（同为2.8%），主要反映私人存货的上调；实际GDP增长主要来自消费支出、出口、联邦政府支出和非住宅固定投资的增长，同时进口（GDP计算中的减项）增加。",
        "kind": "model_interpretation",
        "citations": [
          {
            "source_id": "source_20bd17ab9d75424aafe5b33229d32d43",
            "location": {
              "character_start": 764,
              "character_end": 904,
              "page": 1
            },
            "quotation_match": "whitespace_normalized",
            "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
            "quotation": "In the advance estimate, the increase in real GDP was also 2.8\npercent. The update primarily reflected upward revisions to private inventory"
          },
          {
            "source_id": "source_20bd17ab9d75424aafe5b33229d32d43",
            "location": {
              "character_start": 1123,
              "character_end": 1355,
              "page": 1
            },
            "quotation_match": "whitespace_normalized",
            "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
            "quotation": "The increase in real GDP primarily reflected increases in consumer spending, exports, federal\ngovernment spending, and nonresidential fixed investment. Imports, which are a subtraction in the\ncalculation of GDP, increased (table 2)."
          }
        ],
        "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
        "role": "support",
        "uncited_fact_values": [
          "2.8 percent (annualized, seasonally adjusted)"
        ],
        "suggested_fact_evidence": [
          {
